{"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/nicapotato/mock-financial-project?scriptVersionId=320584018\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"6277ba51-4e8c-4422-8ca1-bc6e3e06ec63","_uuid":"07a7a33c8619156044a75a47802147fe6c155575"},"source":["# Fortune 500: Mock Financial Analysis Project\n","\n","In this latest installation, how to **NOT do statistics on Panel Data!**.\n","\n","The goal of this notebook is to explore some of the things I learned from Hastie and Tibshirani's *Introduction to Statistical Learning*.\n","\n","- Pre-Processing:\n","    - Merging and Matching dataframe\n","    - Subset Data and remove NA for Balanced Panel Data\n","    - \n","- Stepwise Feature Selection\n","\n","**NOT SERIOUS, MERELY TOOL EXPLORATION**\n","\n","## Introduction\n","\n","- Fortune 500 Dataset\n","- Year 2014-2016"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"metadata":{"_cell_guid":"80a8f708-ff26-47ca-8f6a-e9ebe249a255","_uuid":"e95d7a62db4c3e979d97c0afa720ada2b5964a44","execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-19T12:57:31.171495Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-19T12:57:31.169224Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-19T12:57:41.594299Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-19T12:57:41.593256Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["\n","Attaching package: ‘lubridate’\n","\n","The following object is masked from ‘package:base’:\n","\n","    date\n","\n"]}],"source":["library(leaps)\n","library(knitr)\n","library(fmsb)\n","library(ggplot2)\n","library(reshape2)\n","library(lubridate)\n","\n","#LOAD\n","fund <- read.csv(\"../input/fundamentals.csv\", header=T)\n","sprice <- read.csv(\"../input/prices-split-adjusted.csv\", header=T)\n","sec <- read.csv(\"../input/securities.csv\", header=T)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"a10448fc-d913-4719-9a6a-8a6d33a231e8","_uuid":"ca3d6f9714b09ece0999b99fabfddd1f49da5a6c"},"source":["#### Goal and Methodology\n","\n","  The goal of this section is to predict which stocks are undervalued by using substracting our multiple linear model's predicted market capitalization from that of the model, dividing the difference by shares outstanding, then selecting the top 10 results.\n","  \n","#### Model Selection: Best Subset and Size\n","  Using the leaps model, best subset variable selection was conducted with all variables on the training set of year 2014. Then, best model accross different predictor size were compared through MSE of the 2015 test set.\n","\n","  Once size was determined, best variable selection was conducted on the entire dataset, 2014 and 2015, and the best variables were chosen out of the recommended amount.\n","  "]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"metadata":{"_cell_guid":"a2c33237-57af-41bc-9be5-7d0e1f3e5ed6","_uuid":"aa93a651809a4a13725e72f33f487fca86742c84","execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-19T12:57:41.622377Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-19T12:57:41.596619Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-19T12:57:43.934753Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-19T12:57:43.933538Z"}},"outputs":[],"source":["#Creating Yearly Stock Price Mean by Ticker\n","sprice$date <- ymd(sprice$date)\n","sprice$year <- year(sprice$date)\n","annual.sp <- aggregate(close ~ symbol + year, sprice, mean)\n","\n","#Add Industry (From SEC) to fundamentals (FUND)\n","names(sec)[names(sec)==\"Ticker.symbol\"] <- \"Ticker.Symbol\"\n","sec.short <- sec[,c(1,4,5)]\n","data <- merge(fund,sec.short, by=\"Ticker.Symbol\", all.x=TRUE)\n","\n","#Time Parse\n","data$Period.Ending <- ymd(data$Period.Ending)\n","data$endyear <- year(data$Period.Ending)\n","\n","#Add annual split-adj Stock Price to Fundamentals\n","annual.sp$index <- paste(as.character(annual.sp$symbol), annual.sp$year, sep=\" \")\n","data$index <- paste(as.character(data$Ticker.Symbol), data$endyear, sep=\" \")\n","data<- merge(data, annual.sp[,3:4], by = \"index\", all.x=TRUE)\n","names(data)[names(data)==\"close\"] <- \"Stock.p\"\n","names(data)[names(data)==\"GICS.Sector\"] <- \"Industry\"\n","data <- subset(data, endyear > 2012 & endyear < 2016) #Remove Outliers\n","data$Period.Ending <- as.Date(data$Period.Ending)\n","data$Year <- year(data$Period.Ending)\n","\n","data <- data[,c(2,85,81,15,19,20,39,43,22,62,61,65,79,80,84)]\n","data$Effect.of.Exchange.Rate <- NULL\n","data$Market.Cap <- data$Stock.p*data$Estimated.Shares.Outstanding\n","data <- subset(data, Estimated.Shares.Outstanding > 0)\n","\n","#2013 to 2015, FULL DATA\n","data <- subset(data, Year > 2013 & Year < 2016)\n","data <- na.omit(data)\n","data <- subset(data, Industry != \"Telecommunications Services\")\n","data$Industry <- as.factor(as.character(data$Industry))\n","\n","#Since Telecom is too small, Remove from dataset\n","tt <- table(data$Ticker.Symbol)\n","data <- subset(data, Ticker.Symbol %in% names(tt[tt == 2]))\n","data$Ticker.Symbol <- as.factor(as.character(data$Ticker.Symbol))\n","data <- data[,-c(12,14)]\n","\n","load <- data\n","data$X <- NULL\n","nam <- names(data)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"1a600862-5c0b-44da-94e0-f7f37e7e1dad","_uuid":"3dc95ab874a8629ede892a2a3e32bced39137891"},"source":["# Train/Test Split\n","TRAIN on 2014 data, test on 2015. Although not a sound method, hacked my way through this one."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"metadata":{"_cell_guid":"6669ab17-2e12-4081-8afb-e9d2a4051e79","_uuid":"dcd680ad7bcfa20069a233a030ad61f22e06d9a7","execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-19T12:57:43.938097Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-19T12:57:43.93681Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-19T12:57:43.949331Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-19T12:57:43.948263Z"}},"outputs":[],"source":["train <- data$Year==2014 "]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"c455c3fe-c99f-45ca-87ab-c6e65659b426","_uuid":"610dedec73784779427c35d676f20934d92a0fbf"},"sou