, ranked by amount undervalued per share."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":17,"metadata":{"_cell_guid":"d712bb2e-510f-4159-bd04-694436c7c883","_uuid":"a5bf45cf6ab7bc330540a62a978f65f4d29042e8","execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-19T12:57:46.147698Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-19T12:57:46.146346Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-19T12:57:46.156223Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-19T12:57:46.155248Z"}},"outputs":[],"source":["## Add 2016 trend for these stocks"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"64bc0bef-10ce-4cd3-aa45-ed43462232ce","_uuid":"ccdab62ebcf3f52ca3a5ae42d18969dbbf6abcb2"},"source":["#### Conclusion for Linear Regression\n","  Model size with the smallest out of sample MSE is 3, usingthe variables Depreciation, Earnings before interest and tax, and , then conducted best variable selection on the whole data to determine the model."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"0b412f89-ecd2-4d48-b5fd-a02d6572fc59","_uuid":"f8918465130ef4bfd073fc79fd2b3c6170c6a98d"},"source":["## Most Important Variables by Industry\n","\n","  This section will use regression to find the most important predictors by industry. Model variables are selected by out-of-sample MSE, on 2015 test data. Then model is then build on full data with determined variables."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":18,"metadata":{"_cell_guid":"dbf41b25-2146-43be-bf34-6d186e057c7f","_uuid":"0962fc4e2755ae0ad55afa04a3b311e430798e4d","execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-19T12:57:46.16007Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-19T12:57:46.158454Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-19T12:57:46.525131Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-19T12:57:46.52373Z"}},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["\n","\n","|Industry               | Industry.Size|       r^2|      AIC| Observations|\n","|:----------------------|-------------:|---------:|--------:|------------:|\n","|Consumer Discretionary |             1| 0.5252203| 6394.490|          126|\n","|Consumer Staples       |             2| 0.9289214| 2498.681|           50|\n","|Energy                 |             3| 0.8527981| 2962.520|           58|\n","|Financials             |             3| 0.9703627| 4308.686|           88|\n","|Health Care            |             5| 0.7959653| 4237.750|           84|\n","|Industrials            |             4| 0.8773961| 5847.891|          120|\n","|Information Technology |             3| 0.8934888| 5547.632|          108|\n","|Materials              |             1| 0.4909040| 2168.183|           44|\n","|Real Estate            |             1| 0.3496813| 2486.223|           50|\n","|Utilities              |             1| 0.8431860| 2005.566|           42|"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["### Linear Regression by Industry:\n","data <- load\n","data$X <- NULL\n","data$Industry <- as.factor(data$Industry)\n","ind.levels <- levels(data$Industry)\n","ni <- length(levels(data$Industry))\n","\n","data$IND <- as.character(data$Industry)\n","data$IND[data$IND==\"Consumer Discretionary\"] <- 1\n","data$IND[data$IND==\"Consumer Staples\"] <- 2\n","data$IND[data$IND==\"Energy\"] <- 3\n","data$IND[data$IND==\"Financials\"] <- 4\n","data$IND[data$IND==\"Health Care\"] <- 5\n","data$IND[data$IND==\"Industrials\"] <- 6\n","data$IND[data$IND==\"Information Technology\"] <- 7\n","data$IND[data$IND==\"Materials\"] <- 8\n","data$IND[data$IND==\"Real Estate\"] <- 9\n","data$IND[data$IND==\"Utilities\"] <- 10\n","data$IND <- as.numeric(data$IND)\n","\n","#Best Subset and  Cross- Validation BY INDUSTRY\n","set.seed(1)\n","p <- 8\n","data$Industry <- NULL\n","ind.size <- rep(NA, ni)\n","list1 <- list(NA)\n","for(j in 1:ni){\n","  data.ind <- subset(data, data$IND==j) #Subset for Industry\n","  train <- data.ind$Year==2014 #TRAIN\n","  regfit.best<- regsubsets(Market.Cap~.-Ticker.Symbol-Year-IND-Estimated.Shares.Outstanding, data=data.ind[train,],nvmax=p)\n","  test.mat=model.matrix(Market.Cap~.-Ticker.Symbol-Year-IND-Estimated.Shares.Outstanding,data=data.ind[!train,])\n","  val.errors=rep(NA,p)\n","  for(i in 1:p){\n","    coefi=coef(regfit.best, id=i)\n","    pred=test.mat[,names(coefi)]%*%coefi\n","    val.errors[i]=mean((data.ind$Market.Cap[!train]-pred)^2)\n","    }\n","  ind.size[j] <-which.min(val.errors)\n","  regfit.best=regsubsets(Market.Cap~.-Ticker.Symbol-Year-IND-Estimated.Shares.Outstanding,data=data.ind,nvmax =p)\n","  list1[[j]] <- coef(regfit.best ,which.min(val.errors))\n","}\n","\n","#Data.Frame\n","indus <- data.frame(ind.levels, rep(NA,ni), ind.size)\n","indus$variables <- NA\n","for(k in 1:ni){\n","  p <- length(names(list1[[k]]))\n","  indus$variables[k] <- paste(names(list1[[k]][2:p]), collapse=\", \")\n","}\n","\n","#Results:\n","lm.MSE <- list(NA)\n","lm.MSE[[1]] <- lm(Market.Cap~Earnings.Before.Interest.and.Tax, data=subset(data, IND==1))\n","lm.MSE[[2]] <- lm(Market.Cap~Cost.of.Revenue+Net.Income+Profit.Margin, data=subset(data, IND==2))\n","lm.MSE[[3]] <- lm(Market.Cap~Depreciation+Net.Income, data=subset(data, IND==3))\n","lm.MSE[[4]] <- lm(Market.Cap~Cost.of.Revenue+Earnings.Before.Interest.and.Tax+Net.Cash.Flow+\n","                      Net.Income+Profit.Margin, data=subset(data, IND==4))\n","lm.MSE[[5]] <- lm(Market.Cap~Depreciation+Earnings.Before.Interest.and.Tax+Net.Cash.Flow+\n","                      Net.Income+Profit.Margin,data=subset(data, IND==5))\n","lm.MSE[[6]] <- lm(Market.Cap~Cost.of.Revenue+Depreciation+Earnings.Before.Interest.and.Tax+\n","                      Net.Income+Profit.Margin, data=subset(data, IND==6))\n","lm.MSE[[7]] <- lm(Market.Cap~Cost.of.Revenue+Depreciation+Earnings.Before.Interest.and.Tax\n","                    +Net.Income, data=subset(data, IND==7))\n","lm.MSE[[8]] <- lm(Market.Cap~Cost.of.Revenue+Depreciation+Net.Income+\n","                     Pre.Tax.ROE, data=subset(data, IND==8))\n","lm.MSE[[9]] <- lm(Market.Cap~Cost.of.Revenue+Depreciation+Earnings.Before.Interest.and.Tax+\n","                     Net.Income+Profit.Margin, data=subset(data, IND==9))\n","lm.MSE[[10]] <- lm(Market.Cap~Earnings.Before.Interest.and.Tax, data=subset(data, IND==10))\n","\n","indus$r2 <- NA\n","\n","names(indus) <- c(\"Industry\", \"AIC\", \"Industry.Size\", \"Coefficients\", \"r^2\")\n","indus$Observations <- rep(NA,10)\n","for (m in 1:10){\n","  indus[m,5] <- summary(lm.MSE[[m]])$adj.r.squared\n","  indus[m,2] <- AIC(lm.MSE[[m]])\n","  indus[m,6] <- nrow(subset(data, IND==m))\n","}\n","indus<- indus[,c(1,3,4,5,2,6)]\n","\n","kable(indus[,-3])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"c6ec474e-74c4-4b85-a3d9-10466e57b6b4","_uuid":"7aa29e2b71a9c91e684e481e01acb07fd50730d5"},"source":[" It is also evident that some industries are much more predictable than other.However, this may be due to the selection of variables."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":19,"metadata":{"_cell_guid":"4ea1f0b6-3dfc-4623-8242-fa65b72d1c57","_uuid":"673d48635f409d14485d7e2f54014f0cc1cc8173","execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-19T12:57:46.528654Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-19T12:57:46.527414Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-19T12:57:47.254812Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-19T12:57:47.254333Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["`geom_smooth()` using method = 'loess' and formula 'y ~ x'\n","Warning message in simpleLoess(y, x, w, span, degree = degree, parametric = parametric, :\n","“pseudoinverse used at 0.98”Warning message in simpleLoess(y, x, w, span, degree = degree, parametric = parametric, :\n","“neighborhood radius 2.02”Warning message in simpleLoess(y, x, w, span, degree = degree, parametric = parametric, :\n","“reciprocal condition number  0”Warning message in simpleLoess(y, x, w, span, degree = degree, parametric = parametric, :\n","“There are other near singularities as well. 1”"]},{"data":{},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAA0gAAANICAIAAAByhViMAAAABmJLR0QA/wD/AP+gvaeTAAAg\nAElEQVR4nOzdd3gUdf4H8M/ULdn0npACSUhIaKF3EFQQB